---
pagination:
  data: sites.redirects
  size: 1
  alias: redirect
permalink: "{{ redirect.from }}"
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{#
	An address that used to mean something, at the address it used to have.

	Both kinds land here: the original Speedlify's category paths, which this
	instance replaced at the same domain, and any category since folded into
	another.

	A static host has no way to answer with a 301, so this is the substitute: a
	`refresh` of 0 seconds, which browsers follow immediately, plus a canonical
	link so a crawler consolidates the two rather than indexing both. The prose
	is for the case where neither happens — a reader with the meta refresh
	disabled gets a sentence and a link rather than a blank page.

	Deliberately not the site's own layout. It is a doorway, not a page: loading
	the masthead, the stylesheet and the category switcher for something nobody
	sees for more than a moment is work spent on a redirect.
#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url={{ redirect.to }}">
<link rel="canonical" href="{{ meta.url }}{{ redirect.to }}">
<meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">
<title>Moved to {{ redirect.name }}</title>
</head>
<body>
<p>This page has moved to <a href="{{ redirect.to }}">{{ redirect.name }}</a>.</p>
</body>
</html>
